"epic question" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-question&gt;
		<header>A question's text, as first asked, under a small Question label: first in its item.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>A question's text, as first asked. It draws a small grey <text code>QUESTION</> label over the text, and sits first in its item, before the options and the answer.</>

	<!--
		no <ui-list class="spell-meta">:  its <ui-item>s take the "item" style sheet before the pack's
		              <epic-item> can, and the live items draw unstyled (issue I9 of epic-components)
	-->
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone reading or writing an epic page's markup, or changing this element.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph><label size="mini" color="green">built</> in <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-question" link="/epic/src/components/epic-question/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-question/" code>epic-question/</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary (every table below comes from it): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-question-epicquestion-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-question/EpicQuestion.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-question/EpicQuestion.en.ts" code>EpicQuestion.en.ts</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>The markup rules: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-tool-plan-doc-md" link="/epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md"><text title="epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md" code>PLAN-DOC.md</></>.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>Live: the real element, drawn by the epics pack this page loads.</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Click a line to unfold it.</>
			<item>The review buttons don't show here: they show only on an epic page being reviewed.</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>Q21 of the <text code>wwod</> epic, shown open (as it stood before it was answered), and unfolded.</>
		<html>
			<epic-item id="q21" title="Behaviour switches: ALL-CAPS static, or @proto static?" status="open" state="attention" open>
				<epic-question>
					<p>§12 says behaviour switches are ALL-CAPS statics at the top (<code>Match.DEBUG_MATCH_INITIALIZATION</>), and also "prefer <code>@proto static</> for any per-class constant behaviour switch" (<code>@proto static inlineInitialType = false</>).</>
				</>
				<epic-choices>
					<epic-option letter="A" title="Split by who sets it" recommended>
						<p>ALL-CAPS static: a developer / debug switch, set by hand for the whole class tree. <code>@proto static</>: a behaviour a subclass or instance overrides.</>
					</>
					<epic-option letter="B" title="@proto for all">
						<p>Drop the ALL-CAPS switch form.</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>From Q21 of the <text code>wwod</> epic (<link title="epics/wwod/parts/q21.html" target="src-epics-wwod-parts-q21-html" link="/epics/wwod/parts/q21.html"><text code>q21.html</></>): the question, then its options.</>
		<text paragraph>q21.html:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-question
			  ><p>
			    §12 says behaviour switches are ALL-CAPS statics at the top (<code>Match.DEBUG_MATCH_INITIALIZATION</code>), and
			    also "prefer <code>@proto static</code> for any per-class constant behaviour switch" ...
			  </p></epic-question
			>
			<epic-choices>...</epic-choices>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="layer group"/>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its parents:</>
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-item-html" link="/epic-item"><text code>&lt;epic-item&gt;</></>: first among its details, one at most. The tool finds the question by this tag, not by its place.</>
			<item><link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-version-html" link="/epic-version"><text code>&lt;epic-version&gt;</></>: in an item's Original Discussion, when a rewrite of the question moved the old one there</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>Its children:</>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Child</>
				<cell>How many</>
				<cell>What it holds</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>prose</>
				<cell>any number</>
				<cell>The question, as asked.</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="table columns"/>
		<text paragraph>None: it draws the same wherever it is.</>

		<section label="Slots" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>A slot is a place in the drawing that a child goes to: a child with <text code>slot="name"</> goes to that name's place, every other child to the default one (shown as <text italic>default</>).</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Slot</>
					<cell>What goes there</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text italic>default</>
					</>
					<cell>The question, as asked.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>A part is a piece of what the element draws in its shadow root (its own hidden markup), named so a stylesheet can reach it: <text code>epic-question::part(header)</>.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Part</>
					<cell>What it is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>base</>
					</>
					<cell>The label over the text.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>label</>
					</>
					<cell><text code>Question</>, a small grey eyebrow (as an item's <text code>Original question</>).</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="5. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Neutral: no colour of its own. The label is small, grey, bold capitals, the same look as an item's <text code>Original question</> label.</>
			<item>The text is the page's own children, spaced as an item's details are.</>
			<item>It doesn't fold by itself: it folds with its item.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="6. Written by">
		<icon slot="icon" name="terminal"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><text code>plan-doc add &lt;name&gt; question "title" --details html</>: the lead of the HTML (the prose up to its first element or bold label line, such as <text code>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;The options:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</>) goes into an <text code>&lt;epic-question&gt;</>, unless the HTML has one</>
			<item><text code>plan-doc details &lt;name&gt; &lt;Q id&gt; --file html</>, a rewrite of a question's text: the new lead goes into a new one; the old one moves into the Original Discussion with the rest of the old text</>
			<item><text code>--append</> never makes one</>
			<item>older docs: the converter (<text code>plan-doc convert</>), from a question's leading text</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
			<ui-divider></>
			<ui-text class="meta" paragraph>Last checked 2026-10-09 against branch <ui-text code>epic-components</>: the tables are its vocabulary's; the rest from its component, its stylesheet and <ui-link title="epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md" target="src-spell-epic-src-tool-plan-doc-md" link="/epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md"><ui-text code>PLAN-DOC.md</></>.</>
		</>
	</>
